[?2004hroot@1e5d27b22ade:/task# cat /task/input/library_prep_notes.md
[?2004l# Library preparation notes (batch hand-over from the wet lab)

- Batch: 8 specimens of the study, 2 extraction blanks and the mock community standard, extracted on the same day with one kit lot and carried through all steps together.
- 16S rRNA gene copies per microlitre of extract were measured by qPCR before amplification (column `qpcr_16s_copies_per_ul` of the sample sheet).
- Amplification: V4 region, primers 515F / 806R (see `primers.tsv`), 30 cycles, same template volume for every extract. The primer stocks are equimolar mixes of four phased versions per primer, carrying 0, 1, 2 or 3 extra nucleotides 5' of the primer (heterogeneity spacers).
- Library construction: PCR products were cleaned up, end-repaired/A-tailed and the indexed Illumina adapters were added by ligation (PCR-free ligation kit), one index pair per library.
- Libraries were pooled by equal mass regardless of amplicon yield and sequenced on a MiSeq (v2 500-cycle kit, 2 x 250) in a run shared with other amplicon projects of the core. Demultiplexing and adapter removal were done on the instrument; nothing else was done to the reads.
- Mock standard: 8 bacterial strains mixed at equal 16S copy number (`mock_community.tsv`). The two Serinicoccus strains of the standard differ at 1 position(s) of the V4 amplicon.
